# J21 — Recommend-then-authorize screens (screen-composition redesign)
#
# Walks the new composition screens over the deterministic phase fixture and
# asserts each recommendation card states why, what it will run, the evidence
# it should produce, and the safety boundary BEFORE anything launches:
#   Prove `v`  — bounded investigation plan (3g)
#   Prove `t`  — full-screen trace evidence (3j)
#   Review `C` — attack-chain artifacts (3h)
#   `/full`    — threat-model-seeded configure card (3b)
# The offline demo activates via the `demo` command; the fixture then seeds on
# scan completion. Numeric page keys are printable view hotkeys, so this
# journey toggles nav mode with Esc (empty prompt) before page selection.
# The configure card is Map-first by design: `/full` without an accepted
# current-revision Map routes through the Map plan, the operator authorizes a
# context-only Map run (Build threat model toggled off — no model is configured), and the
# re-entered guided flow shows the threat-model-seeded SCAN · MODULES card.
name: Recommend-then-authorize screens
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
keys: Escape
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 PDF phase reference fixture loaded
submit: workbench
wait: 2
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Prove | 1-prove
expect: STATUS / NEXT
expect: PROOF SUBJECT · finding
keys: v
wait-live-snap: 10 INVESTIGATE · Enter draft command | 2-investigation-plan
expect: EVIDENCE GOALS
expect: SAFETY BOUNDARY
expect: STOP CONDITIONS
expect: nothing runs until you submit the drafted command
ask: Investigate — does the plan state why, evidence goals, boundary, and stop conditions with a drafted command and no auto-launch?
keys: v
wait: 1
keys: t
wait-live-snap: 10 TRACE · Enter draft trace:expand | 3-trace
expect: RECORDED PATH
expect: EXPANDED PATH · requested by operator
expect: run trace:expand
ask: Trace — is the recorded path clearly separated from operator-requested expansion, with Enter only drafting the command?
keys: t
wait: 1
nav-mode:
keys: 3
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Review | 4-review
expect: SELECTED FINDING
nav-mode:
keys: C
wait-live-snap: 10 ATTACK CHAINS · Enter open constituent | 5-attack-chains
expect: ATTACK CHAINS
expect: C-0001
ask: Chains — are chains rendered as artifacts over constituent findings (assumptions, prerequisites) rather than a bare visualization?
keys: C
wait: 1
keys: Escape
submit: /full
wait-live-snap: 15 MAP · ROUTE | 6-map-route
expect: Map establishes the target context Scan engines will consume.
expect: RECOMMENDED
ask: Map-first — does the guided flow refuse to configure Scan without an accepted Map, recommending the Map plan instead of silently skipping?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 MAP · MODULES
keys: 5
wait: 1
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 STEP 3 OF 3
keys: a
wait-live-snap: 60 RESULT READY | 7-map-result-ready
expect: Use map & choose Scan modules
ask: Result gate — does the completed Map stop with a receipt and recommend (not auto-run) the hand-off to Scan?
keys: Enter
wait-live-snap: 15 Seeded by | 8-configure-scan
expect: Seeded by the threat model
expect: RECOMMENDED
ask: Configure — is the plan seeded from the threat model with per-row rationales, and does nothing run before the explicit commit action?
keys: Escape
